msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-board.rst:26
#: 2150db1aa2d447d8ba8f936f006c01d1
msgid "The main camera control protocol used is known as PTP (Picture Transfer Protocol), which was originally standardized as PIMA 15740:2000, ISO 15740:2005(V1.0), and ISO 15740:2008(V1.1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-board.rst:30
#: 02f7ae976b044d33a35eb020496fc793
msgid "The PTP has been supported by almost all cameras since 2005, but often in a limited fashion. Only few cameras have the \"PTP Remote Control\" feature. Canon, for example, removed the remote control feature from their compact line (PowerShot models) in the last PS SDK in 2009 (PS-ReCSDK 1.1.0e)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-board.rst:36
#: cb80af67337d48259b30f040ce9807a3
msgid "Fortunately the PTP hacking extension in the `CHDK project <http://chdk.wikia.com/wiki/PTP_Extension>`__ allows us to extend the PTP control to newer, smaller and lighter Canon PowerShot models."
msgstr ""

